In May 2012, after successfully auditioning for [[The X Factor (British TV series)|''The X Factor'' (UK)]], [[Ella Henderson]], then 16 years old, performed a ballad arrangement of "Believe" after the Bootcamp round, reducing guest judge [[Nicole Scherzinger]] to tears.<ref>{{Citation |title=Ella Henderson's performance - Cher's Believe - The X Factor UK 2012 | date=September 23, 2012 |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oTbcO9qaE5g |language=en |access-date=November 15, 2022}}</ref> The cover, which was based on [[Adam Lambert]]'s version performed on ''[[American Idol]]'' in 2009,<ref>{{Citation |title=Turning back time: Adam Lambert performed that 'Believe' cover on American Idol |url=https://ew.com/tv/2018/12/27/adam-lambert-believe-cher-american-idol/ |language=en |access-date=December 11, 2022}}</ref> was so popular for its slow tempo, emotional interpretation that Henderson released an acoustic performance in 2013 on [[YouTube]]<ref>{{Citation |title=Ella Henderson : Believe (Cher Cover) | date=January 27, 2013 |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rMY6FUkCfaw |language=en |access-date=November 15, 2022}}</ref> and performed it at the [[National Television Awards]] on January 23, 2013.<ref>{{Citation |title=Ella Henderson performs "Believe" at the National Television Awards 2013 (23rd January) | date=January 23, 2013 |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ads-_fZZpcQ |language=en |access-date=November 15, 2022}}</ref> Henderson also included a studio version of the cover on a deluxe edition of her debut album ''[[Chapter One (Ella Henderson album)|Chapter One]]'' as part of a pre-order EP called ''Chapter One Sessions''.{{Citation needed|date=September 2025}}

In October 2016, the Australian rock band [[DMA's]] performed "Believe" for [[Triple J]]'s ''[[Like a Version]]''. It made such an impact on the Australian audience that in the year it was performed, the cover became the highest ranked Like A Version in a [[Triple J Hottest 100|Hottest 100]] countdown, landing at number 6 in the [[Triple J Hottest 100, 2016|2016 edition]] of the countdown (this was later surpassed by [[The Wiggles]] in [[Triple J Hottest 100, 2021|2021]]). In 2020 it was the only Like A Version to feature in the [[Triple J Hottest 100 of the 2010s|Hottest 100 of the 2010s]] countdown landing at No. 41. In 2023, it topped the [[Triple J Hottest 100 of Like a Version]] countdown.<ref>{{Citation |title=Believe it: How DMA'S covering Cher became your #1 Like A Version of all time |url=https://www.abc.net.au/triplej/programs/hack/dmas-cher-believe-like-a-version-hottest-100/102606354 |language=en |date=July 15, 2023|access-date=November 4, 2023}}</ref>

In December 2018, Lambert performed his ballad version of "Believe" again in honor of Cher during the 41st annual [[Kennedy Center Honors]]; the performance was highly acclaimed, with Cher stating that she was "at a loss for words" and was moved to tears.<ref>{{cite magazine|url=https://www.billboard.com/music/pop/adam-lambert-kennedy-center-honors-ballad-believe-cher-8491620/|title=Adam Lambert and Cyndi Lauper Tribute Cher at Kennedy Center Honors: Watch the Performances|magazine=Billboard|date=December 27, 2018|access-date=July 5, 2020}}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine|url=https://www.billboard.com/music/pop/cher-reacts-adam-lambert-kennedy-center-performance-8491630/|title=Cher 'Overwhelmed,' Moved to Tears by Adam Lambert's Kennedy Center Honors Performance|magazine=Billboard|date=December 27, 2018|access-date=July 5, 2020}}</ref> On December 6, 2019, Lambert released a studio version of his version of "Believe", which reached number 23 on the ''Billboard'' [[Digital Songs|Digital Song Sales]] chart on December 21, 2019.<ref>{{cite magazine|url=https://www.billboard.com/music/pop/adam-lambert-releases-cover-cher-believe-8545590/|title=Adam Lambert Finally Released His Spine-Tingling Cover of Cher's 'Believe': Listen|magazine=Billboard|date=December 6, 2019|access-date=July 5, 2020}}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine|url=https://www.billboard.com/charts/digital-song-sales/2019-12-21|title=DIGITAL SONG SALES, The week of December 21, 2019|magazine=Billboard|date=January 2, 2013|access-date=July 5, 2020}}</ref>

sections.text:
In May 2012, after successfully auditioning for The X Factor (UK), Ella Henderson, then 16 years old, performed a ballad arrangement of "Believe" after the Bootcamp round, reducing guest judge Nicole Scherzinger to tears. The cover, which was based on Adam Lambert's version performed on American Idol in 2009, was so popular for its slow tempo, emotional interpretation that Henderson released an acoustic performance in 2013 on YouTube and performed it at the National Television Awards on January 23, 2013. Henderson also included a studio version of the cover on a deluxe edition of her debut album Chapter One as part of a pre-order EP called Chapter One Sessions.{{Citation needed|date=September 2025}}

In October 2016, the Australian rock band DMA's performed "Believe" for Triple J's Like a Version. It made such an impact on the Australian audience that in the year it was performed, the cover became the highest ranked Like A Version in a Hottest 100 countdown, landing at number 6 in the 2016 edition of the countdown (this was later surpassed by The Wiggles in 2021). In 2020 it was the only Like A Version to feature in the Hottest 100 of the 2010s countdown landing at No. 41. In 2023, it topped the Triple J Hottest 100 of Like a Version countdown.

In December 2018, Lambert performed his ballad version of "Believe" again in honor of Cher during the 41st annual Kennedy Center Honors; the performance was highly acclaimed, with Cher stating that she was "at a loss for words" and was moved to tears. On December 6, 2019, Lambert released a studio version of his version of "Believe", which reached number 23 on the Billboard Digital Song Sales chart on December 21, 2019.

